{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Of laughter.</b> I said that לִשְׂחוֹק ( laughter) is that it is מְהוֹלָל (madness), and he said concerning joy: what does it do, what does it profit, and what good does it produce, and the lamed is like the lamed in לְמַד (instruct) — [as in] they said to me, my brother, it is he — and he said, the deliverance of the children of Israel."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "פרע׳ is likely an abbreviation for פְּרֵעַ or פְּדוּת (deliverance); the cryptic parenthetical citation to a verse with למ״ד cannot be identified with certainty."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:27:02.586961021Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}